# Copy to .env and fill in. .env is gitignored — never commit real tokens.
# See README.md step 1 for where each of these comes from.

# vast.ai account API key — https://cloud.vast.ai/manage-keys/
# Required by spin_up.py (it rents the instance). Optional for the server
# itself, where it only enables the in-UI "Shut down instance" button.
#
# Keys default to FULL account access. Restrict at creation ("+New" on the
# Keys page) — spin_up.py needs exactly this much of the permission grid:
#
#   User             Read        read-only identity
#   Instances        Read        GET    /instances/       poll until running
#   Instances        Write       PUT    /asks/{id}/       rent it
#                                DELETE /instances/{id}/  destroy it
#   Miscellaneous    Enabled     POST   /bundles/         find offers
#   Billing/Earning  leave OFF
#   Team             leave OFF
#
# Miscellaneous is load-bearing despite the name: without it the offer search
# comes back empty and spin_up.py never finds a GPU to rent.
#
# Billing stays OFF even though renting spends money — creating an instance is
# an Instances:Write action, and the billing scopes only cover invoices and
# credit. So the key can spend your balance but cannot inspect or alter it.
#
# CLI equivalent:
#   vastai create api-key --name roscommon --permissions \
#     '{"api": {"misc": {}, "user_read": {}, "instance_read": {}, "instance_write": {}}}'
VAST_API_KEY=

# Hugging Face READ token — https://huggingface.co/settings/tokens
# Accept the license for each model in models.json first:
#   https://huggingface.co/kyutai/personaplex-rl-seamless   (loaded at boot)
#   https://huggingface.co/nvidia/personaplex-7b-v1
HF_TOKEN=

# OPTIONAL — a prompt of your own, for whatever this deployment is demoing.
# spin_up.py forwards it to the instance, where it becomes the prompt the UI
# opens with, highlighted as the "Customized" preset next to the built-in
# examples. Leave it blank and the UI opens on its own default prompt instead;
# 8 characters or fewer counts as blank.
#
# One line only (this file is read line by line, so a newline ends the value),
# and no surrounding quotes are needed — they're stripped if you add them.
SYSTEM_PROMPT=
